NAME
       setfiles - set SELinux file contexts from a context list

SYNOPSIS
       setfiles [-v] [-n] [-F] SPEC-FILE PATH...

DESCRIPTION
       setfiles is the tool behind restorecon and the full relabel at boot:
       it labels the files under each PATH from the rules in SPEC-FILE (the
       policy's file_contexts). For everyday work use restorecon, which
       finds the policy's list by itself and needs no SPEC-FILE.

OPTIONS
       -v     Show the files whose context changes.

       -n     Change nothing.

       -F     Reset the whole context, not only the type.

EXAMPLES
           setfiles -v /etc/selinux/targeted/contexts/files/file_contexts /srv

SEE ALSO
       restorecon(8), fixfiles(8), semanage(8)
